1 REM ============================================================
2 REM  t63_mat_operations.bpp
3 REM  BASIC++ MAT (Matrix) Operations Test & Tutorial
4 REM ============================================================
5 REM
6 REM  MAT operations come from ECMA-55/116 Minimal/Full BASIC.
7 REM  They provide array-wide operations in a single statement.
8 REM
9 REM  SUPPORTED MAT OPERATIONS:
10 REM    MAT READ A      - Fill array A from DATA
11 REM    MAT PRINT A     - Print entire array
12 REM    MAT A = ZER      - Fill A with zeros
13 REM    MAT A = CON      - Fill A with ones
14 REM    MAT A = IDN      - Set A to identity matrix
15 REM    MAT A = B        - Copy B into A
16 REM    MAT A = B + C    - Element-wise add
17 REM    MAT A = B - C    - Element-wise subtract
18 REM    MAT A = (k)*B    - Scalar multiply
19 REM    MAT A = B * C    - Matrix multiply
20 REM    MAT A = TRN(B)   - Transpose
21 REM    MAT A = INV(B)   - Inverse
22 REM
23 DIALECT "E55"
24 REM
100 REM === MAT ZER - Zero fill ===
101 REM MAT A = ZER fills all elements of array A with 0.
110 TEST "MAT ZER"
120 DIM A(5)
130 MAT A = ZER
140 ASSERT A(1)=0
150 ASSERT A(3)=0
160 ASSERT A(5)=0
170 ENDTEST
200 REM === MAT CON - Fill with ones ===
201 REM MAT A = CON fills all elements of array A with 1.
210 TEST "MAT CON"
220 DIM B(5)
230 MAT B = CON
240 ASSERT B(1)=1
250 ASSERT B(3)=1
260 ASSERT B(5)=1
270 ENDTEST
300 REM === MAT READ from DATA ===
301 REM MAT READ A reads values from DATA statements
302 REM into array A, filling element by element.
310 TEST "MAT READ"
320 DIM C(3)
330 MAT READ C
340 ASSERT C(1)=10
350 ASSERT C(2)=20
360 ASSERT C(3)=30
370 ENDTEST
380 DATA 10, 20, 30
400 REM === MAT array copy ===
401 REM MAT A = B copies all elements of B into A.
410 TEST "MAT copy"
420 DIM D(3)
430 MAT D = C
440 ASSERT D(1)=10
450 ASSERT D(2)=20
460 ASSERT D(3)=30
470 ENDTEST
500 REM === MAT PRINT ===
501 REM MAT PRINT A displays all elements of the array.
510 TEST "MAT PRINT"
520 MAT PRINT C
530 REM Should print: 10 20 30
540 ENDTEST
9999 END
